Package: glpsol
Type: Package
Title: Bundled 'GLPK' Solver for 'MathProg', 'LP' and 'MPS' Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Oleg", family = "Lugovoy",
           email = "olugovoy@optimalsolution.dev",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5546-9875")),
    person(given = "Free Software Foundation, Inc.",
           role = "cph",
           comment = "src/glpk/glpsol.c from 'GLPK' 5.0, see inst/COPYRIGHTS"))
Description: Ships the 'glpsol' stand-alone solver of the GNU Linear
    Programming Kit ('GLPK') with R and runs it as a separate process with a
    time limit and an optional live log. 'glpsol' reads 'MathProg' (GMPL)
    models with separate data files, CPLEX LP and MPS files, and solves them
    with the simplex, interior-point or branch-and-cut methods, writing the
    solution to a file. Windows and macOS binary builds carry a static copy
    of 'GLPK'; other platforms link against the system library.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: GLPK (>= 5.0): libglpk-dev (deb), glpk-devel (rpm),
    glpk (brew)
URL: https://github.com/optimal2050/glpsol
BugReports: https://github.com/optimal2050/glpsol/issues
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
